8\. Valid tokens fail after token growth <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code>

<pre>
<b><i>verifyRuntimeToken</i></b> loads an unordered, hard-limited set of 1,000 service-token rows and searches
only that truncated set for the supplied hash instead of querying the indexed token hash directly.
Once storage exceeds 1,000 records, valid unrevoked tokens outside the adapter-selected page are
treated as invalid, with database ordering determining which tokens remain usable.
</pre>


<details>
<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>

```
## Issue description
Runtime-token verification scans an arbitrary, hard-limited page of service-token records, so valid tokens can become unverifiable once the table exceeds 1,000 rows.

## Fix Focus Areas
- secfn/server/src/vault.ts[701-715]
- secfn/server/src/vault.ts[735-754]
- secfn/core/src/schema.ts[125-127]
- secfn/core/src/schema.ts[141-163]

## Recommended Fix
Query `secfn_service_tokens` directly using the indexed deterministic token hash instead of loading and scanning a limited candidate list. Perform constant-time verification on the single matching record, then preserve the revoked, expiry, and scope checks.
