11\. Tenants can read each other's traces <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code>

<pre>
The <b><i>/traces</i></b> handler obtains authenticated tenant context but passes only caller-selected provider,
model, and limit filters through <b><i>LangFn.getTraces</i></b>, while shared trace storage applies no tenant
predicate and feedback looks up arbitrary trace IDs without ownership validation. Because
completion, chat, and stream routes attach tenant context to trace metadata, any authenticated
tenant can enumerate other tenants’ recorded prompts, outputs, errors, and metadata or submit
feedback against their traces.
