# Reject contradictory runtime scope representations

## Affected sites
- `secfn/server/src/router.ts:383-387` — combines caller-supplied IDs with query- or context-derived names.
- `secfn/server/src/vault.ts:760-765` — resolves by ID whenever present and ignores the corresponding name.
- `secfn/server/src/vault.ts:894-926` — ID lookups enforce tenant/namespace ownership but do not compare a concurrently supplied canonical name.

## Required outcome
- When both forms are present, namespace and environment IDs must resolve to the same canonical scope as their supplied names before token verification or secret access.

## Suggested approach
- Resolve the ID, normalize the supplied name, and reject any mismatch before returning the canonical scope.
